1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,060
Look carefully with your heart

2
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:36,039
Find the truth right beside you

3
00:00:36,039 --> 00:00:39,060
Hey you good or bad, truth or lies

4
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,039
Can't escape this heart's gray haze

5
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:45,039
Bring all your courage

6
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:48,200
And maybe save this world

7
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,420
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

8
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:53,780
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

9
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:56,760
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

10
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:57,980
Mojo Spy

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,799
The Sound of Lament

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,640
[Readout ---- complete]

13
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,640
MY FISH BASIN!!!

14
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,640
No!!!

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,780
So it is The Illumin-Eye

16
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:18,900
Uncle!

17
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:27,439
Everyone who lost their voice participated in

18
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:29,259
a recording of the TV show 'Treasure Match'

19
00:02:29,259 --> 00:02:30,560
I'm certain

20
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:34,179
This is definitely not a coincidence

21
00:02:34,179 --> 00:02:37,340
There must be some connection between the two!

22
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:45,359
Uncle

23
00:02:45,359 --> 00:02:48,479
I shouldn't have snuck into your secret room to get the files

24
00:02:48,479 --> 00:02:51,099
But I wanted to prove I'm not just a troublemaker

25
00:02:59,259 --> 00:03:02,060
I knew that no matter what method

26
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,000
Nothing can lock away a little detective's curiosity

27
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,699
So I deliberately left the key to the secret room at home

28
00:03:07,699 --> 00:03:10,840
I also wanted to see what you could actually dig up

29
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,060
Really?

30
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:16,079
And this time your deduction was right on the money

31
00:03:16,079 --> 00:03:18,419
Uncle~

32
00:03:18,419 --> 00:03:20,000
Of course

33
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,620
Uncle, you're really annoying

34
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,180
So you set all this up

35
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:24,759
Don't ever underestimate me again

36
00:03:24,759 --> 00:03:26,739
Officer Han

37
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:29,659
Let's show the little detective how the case is going

38
00:03:29,659 --> 00:03:30,520
Shall we?

39
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:30,860
Sure

40
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:35,159
As Locky said

41
00:03:35,159 --> 00:03:37,700
Several guests at the day-before-yesterday's Treasure Match recording

42
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,560
lost their voices one after another

43
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,719
And before they lost their voices

44
00:03:41,719 --> 00:03:45,400
the treasures they showed on the program

45
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,300
were each stolen as well

46
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:50,000
As Locky Qi said

47
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,200
The lost treasures and the stolen voices

48
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,960
must have some kind of connection

49
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:58,820
But now the strange thing is

50
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:01,620
after stealing the treasures

51
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:05,420
They return to the owner and destroy the treasure

52
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:08,100
That's what baffles me

53
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:11,760
They're not after the treasure

54
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,800
It's you again, you freak!

55
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,100
What are you here to mess up now?

56
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:25,819
They don't want the treasure

57
00:04:25,819 --> 00:04:29,040
But when the owner sees their beloved treasure destroyed,

58
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,019
the desperate screams they let out

59
00:04:31,019 --> 00:04:43,680
The Illumin-Eye

60
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:48,000
Can't believe it's these guys again

61
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,959
Was stealing Miss MU's voice last time not enough?

62
00:04:50,959 --> 00:04:53,600
Now they're going after others again

63
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:57,120
But why would they steal so many voices at once?

64
00:04:57,120 --> 00:05:00,200
The Illumin-Eye never plays by the rules

65
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,920
Every crime they commit is utterly bizarre

66
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:06,180
We can't figure out their pattern now

67
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:11,879
According to the order of guests on the Treasure Appraisal Match TV show,

68
00:05:11,879 --> 00:05:15,340
The Illumin-Eye's next target should be Firecracker Long

69
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:20,480
I've already sent Inspector Sima to hide out at Firecracker Long's house

70
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:23,980
This time we won't let them succeed so easily

71
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:26,460
Hello?

72
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,500
What?

73
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,259
Firecracker Long's treasure has already been stolen

74
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:38,020
The next guest sharing their treasure is Mr. Firecracker Long

75
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,280
Hello, Mr. Firecracker Long

76
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:43,420
Now, please show everyone your treasure.

77
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:47,200
My treasure is nothing special—

78
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:50,100
It's a special love-filled firework I made myself.

79
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:54,100
So why did you make such a love-filled firework?

80
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:58,960
Well, for various reasons,

81
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:01,280
my wife and I have been having disagreements.

82
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:04,200
Even though they're trivial matters,

83
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,580
neither of us is willing to make the first move.

84
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:10,060
So I put all my apologies and love for my wife

85
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:14,960
into this love-filled firework.

86
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:18,680
I plan to set it off at the fireworks festival in a few days.

87
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:23,319
I hope my wife can hear what I have to say to her.

88
00:06:23,319 --> 00:06:24,920
So we can reconcile.

89
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,319
Mr. Long,

90
00:06:26,319 --> 00:06:28,300
you are so thoughtful.

91
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:31,960
I'm truly happy that your wife has such a good husband.

92
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:32,680
I think

93
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:36,379
you two will surely make up.

94
00:06:36,379 --> 00:06:36,980
So,

95
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:41,860
could you show everyone your treasure today?

96
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,259
No, no, no.

97
00:06:43,259 --> 00:06:44,800
This precious firework

98
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,879
holds my most precious feelings.

99
00:06:46,879 --> 00:06:48,660
Before it's set off,

100
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:51,820
I won't show it to anyone.

101
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:55,580
I hid it in the most secret place in my house

102
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:58,280
A place no one would ever think of

103
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:01,040
A place you'd never guess in a million years

104
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,900
Go on, guess where

105
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:10,340
I hid it in our fridge

106
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:11,780
What do you think?

107
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:13,460
Pretty sneaky, right?

108
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:17,720
I never told a soul about this secret

109
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,720
So don't you go telling anyone either

110
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:31,720
That must be one beautiful firework

111
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:34,720
Dottie

112
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,720
The last treasure is already ours

113
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,720
Now all we need to do is take it...

114
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:44,720
Oh stop it, Dottie

115
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,720
Don't look at me like that

116
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:55,140
Too perfect~

117
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:58,580
I've never seen such a perfect work of art

118
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:02,780
It's just a firework, isn't it?

119
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:03,680
What's the big deal?

120
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,420
No

121
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,780
This isn't just an ordinary firework

122
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:08,740
This is a perfect work of art

123
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:10,060
Its color

124
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:10,940
Its texture

125
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,740
Its design — absolutely flawless

126
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,080
Most importantly,

127
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,860
it contains within it

128
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:19,060
the infinite love that created this couple.

129
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:23,360
All the so-called beauty in this world

130
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:26,100
will turn to dust before it.

131
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:27,379
Perfect!

132
00:08:27,379 --> 00:08:28,340
Perfect!

133
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,840
Perfect!

134
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:37,879
For Love and Ideals!

135
00:08:37,879 --> 00:08:42,340
How is the mission going?

136
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:48,340
Flawless, Lord Eye.

137
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:49,500
As you wish.

138
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:52,860
Everything has gone smoothly with this mission.

139
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:55,440
I'm confident it will be completed very soon.

140
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,100
As you wish,

141
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:58,080
my Lord Eye.

142
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,580
Now only the last voice remains to be collected.

143
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:03,120
Then we can synthesize a lament to replace

144
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,180
Sleeping Beauty's heavenly voice.

145
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:09,259
Hmm. A three-legged cat won't eat a rat-poisoned mouse

146
00:09:09,259 --> 00:09:11,539
twice.

147
00:09:11,539 --> 00:09:13,279
This time, you must succeed.

148
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:14,740
You must not fail.

149
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:17,740
For Love and Ideals!

150
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:21,740
For Love and Ideals!

151
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:27,740
Ugh, I'm done~

152
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,740
Dottie

153
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,740
We just need to take this passionate firework

154
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,740
and destroy it right in front of its owner.

155
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,740
Then the mission is complete.

156
00:09:44,740 --> 00:10:14,720
All alone, lonely and blue,

157
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:18,419
the horizon waves to me, too.

158
00:10:18,419 --> 00:10:22,080
Day after day, from sunrise to sunset,

159
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:26,080
spinning through time, dreaming more.

160
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:31,100
Yearning for every second and moment of life,

161
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:37,820
my bright eyes sparkle and shine.

162
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:41,180
A smile that greets the sunlight,

163
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:46,420
it's no secret—right at the corner of Qian'an's house.